// Pseudo idempotent sink
function ingestEvent(event, store) {
  const key = event.device_id + ':' + event.nonce;
  if (store.exists(key)) return;
  store.write(key, event.score);
  // update region aggregates atomically
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test replay protection under clock skew?
- How would you validate exactly-once semantics across partitions?

## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses the ability to design privacy-first multi-tenant experimentation systems with minimal attack surface while maintaining reproducible results.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation through data masking and per-tenant encryption keys
- Feature flags for A/B testing while preserving privacy
- Reproducible scoring and safe rollback mechanisms

## Code Example
```javascript
// Derive user token per tenant and mask IDs to prevent cross-tenant correlation
function maskId(id, tenantKey) {
  return crypto.createHmac('sha256', tenantKey).update(id).digest('hex');
}

// Example usage
